> On 09.04.2011 21:51, Patric Mueller wrote:
>> Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
>>> I wonder why in UnNethack, if hitting with a god-granted artifact, you
>>> get the message that you're doing something wrong using that weapon.
>> 
>> Since when do NH gods care about the players. He just threw you a bone
>> in the hope that you aren't a nuisance anymore. :)
>
> Well, okay, sure. Mind to elaborate anyway?

The Gods in NetHack are not really that into the player. Sure they
sometimes help him/her a bit and even from time to time grant a gift
or two.

But the gods don't invest a lot into the player. In NetHack the god
might even forget what role the player is as e.g. nothing keeps the
god from granting lots of spellbooks to a Valkyrie.

Or crowing has already been described years ago as "stfu already" from
your god as it increases the prayer timeout considerably.

Compare this to Crawl where the gods really tend to get attached to
the player the further it progresses. Have you ever felt in NetHack
that your god is "exalted" about your actions? The ultimate god in
this regard is probably Xom where the player might ascend to the rang
of "a beloved toy of Xom".


This is of course can be explained as the god code is not that complex
and diversified as in Crawl but this can also be explained in in-game
terms that the gods don't really care about the players.

And useless gifts perfectly fit this view.

